cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Equity Lens: a transparency tool for selection committees"
message: "If you use Equity Lens in your work, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Equity Lens is an open-source, privacy-preserving transparency tool that makes
  structural patterns in a candidate pool visible to a selection committee before
  it decides. It flags gender balance, institutional concentration, career
  interruptions and impact beyond citation metrics, offers an optional
  double-blind mode, and supports private voting in which the pairing between a
  committee member and their ballot is never stored. It does not rank candidates,
  recommend outcomes, or replace human judgment.
